 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Classic old building. Two step solutions. First, get him standing on a solid surface. Fair. Have someone stand at the top of the stairs, he can see them, and hold his arm really tight. Walk him down the stairs like that. Yes, with four legs on each side and a few people standing in the middle. It turns the stairway into a smooth curving path. Keep the conversation light and friendly. Talk about the view, the kitchen, anything he wants to hear. Most of all, be patient and keep him moving forward.",
